From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChristosNtokos <chrisdokos1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8822ce: turn on the driver's silent reset

Every 2 s, xmit_status_check() reads REG_TXDMA_STATUS. When it is
non-zero, it calls rtw_hal_sreset_reset() to recover. NVIDIA's
autoconf.h leaves DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_RESET inside a comment, so
sreset_reset() compiles to an empty function. A TX DMA error then
stays set until the module is reloaded or the board is power-cycled.
The radio still receives but cannot send, and every association
attempt fails.

Seen on a Jetson Orin Nano devkit: REG_TXDMA_STATUS=0x00000c00
(UNKNOWN_QSEL | EP_QSEL_DIFF), 161 failed associations in an hour,
fixed only by a power cycle.

Define DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_RESET. sreset_reset() then stops the
interface, power-cycles the MAC through IPS (the same path the driver
uses for idle power save), and restores the association and keys.

What else the define turns on in this build (PCI, no concurrent mode):
- sreset_inprogress() reports the real flag, so the TX queue is not
  woken and BT-coex notifications are skipped while a reset runs.
- drv_conf.h forces CONFIG_IPS, which CONFIG_POWER_SAVING already sets.
- The firmware-hang check (H2C mailbox not read: "fw read cmd failed")
  now also resets, through linked_status_check().
- rtw_iface_bcmc_sec_cam_map_restore() is compiled but has no caller
  without CONFIG_CONCURRENT_MODE.
- The USB-only and concurrent-mode branches stay compiled out.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: ChristosNtokos <chrisdokos1@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/autoconf.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/autoconf.h b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/autoconf.h
index 9d0858e..d46371f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/autoconf.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/include/autoconf.h
@@ -286,9 +286,10 @@
 #define CONFIG_DBG_COUNTER
 
 #define DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_DETECT
+/* Without this, sreset_reset() is empty and a TX DMA error is never cleared. */
+#define DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_RESET
 /*
 #define DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_DETECT_INT
-#define DBG_CONFIG_ERROR_RESET
 
 #define DBG_IO
 #define DBG_DELAY_OS
